 "contributor": null, "rationale": "Grounding self-critique in external retrieval measurably reduced a checkable hallucination: novelty score on known-non-novel ideas dropped from 6.14/10 to 2.38/10."}, {"id": "26cosci_same_family_judge_bias", "label": "Same-family-judge circularity concern", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "26cosci.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The same Gemini-based Ranking/Reflection agents that generate hypotheses also judge them via simulated debate, so an unsaturating Elo curve reflects self-consistency with the system's own criteria, not independent ground truth (paper's own caption concedes this)."}, {"id": "26cosci_frontier_model_comparison", "label": "Co-Scientist vs frontier reasoning models (Fig. 2b)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "26cosci.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Competitor hypotheses (OpenAI o1/o3-mini-high, DeepSeek R1, Gemini variants) judged using Co-Scientist's own Elo tournament, closer to a home-field advantage than a neutral bake-off."}, {"id": "26cosci_human_expert_evaluation", "label": "Blinded human expert preference/novelty/impact evaluation (Fig. 2c, n=11)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "26cosci.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": null}, {"id": "26cosci_aml_drug_repurposing", "label": "AML drug-repurposing and combination validation", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "26cosci.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": null}, {"id": "26cosci_liver_fibrosis_targets", "label": "Liver fibrosis epigenetic target validation", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "26cosci.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author"